---
const review = [
  ['Buying entry', 'Ivalua describes purchasing that can combine hosted and PunchOut catalog items in a requisition. Confirm where this buyer exposes the supplier link.'],
  ['Supplier catalog', 'Map the buyer to the intended Shopify or Shopify Plus store, collections and catalog access in PunchOut Central.'],
  ['Protocol exchange', 'Request the buyer’s actual PunchOut specification and confirm whether its connection uses cXML or OCI before configuring credentials and cart return.'],
  ['Order handoff', 'Test returned requisition lines, buyer approval and the approved PO channel. The PO, not cart return, creates the Shopify order.']
];
---
<main>
  <section class="page-hero page-hero--mint" id="overview"><div class="wrap page-hero__grid">
    <div class="page-hero__copy reveal"><span class="ey">Shopify Ivalua PunchOut</span><h1>Plan an Ivalua PunchOut connection to Shopify.</h1><p class="lead">Ivalua includes PunchOut catalogs in its buyer purchasing experience. PunchOut Central can use your existing Shopify catalog as the supplier side; the buyer’s protocol, catalog entry and approved-PO channel need to be confirmed for the particular Ivalua environment.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Discuss an Ivalua buyer &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="#details">Review requirements &darr;</a></div></div>
    <div class="hero-visual logo-hero reveal"><div class="hero-visual__label"><span>Buyer system</span><b>Configuration review</b></div><div class="logo-hero__mark"><strong>Ivalua</strong></div><span class="logo-hero__status">PunchOut Central</span><h3>Ivalua to Shopify</h3><p>Confirm buyer-side protocol and document channels.</p></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec" id="flow"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">Ivalua buying path</span><h2>Fit a supplier-hosted catalog into the buyer’s requisition.</h2><p class="lead">Ivalua describes a buying experience that can include hosted and PunchOut catalog items in one requisition. The PunchOut cart must return to the buyer process before approval and ordering.</p></div>
    <div class="integration-flow reveal"><div class="integration-node"><strong>Ivalua</strong><span>Buyer requisition</span></div><div class="integration-arrow">&rarr;</div><div class="integration-node integration-node--accent"><strong>PunchOut Central</strong><span>Buyer-specific connection</span></div><div class="integration-arrow">&rarr;</div><div class="integration-node"><strong>Shopify</strong><span>Supplier-hosted catalog</span></div></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec soft" id="details"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Onboarding questions</span><h2>Get the Ivalua buyer’s integration specification first.</h2><p class="lead">Ivalua buyers can configure purchasing differently. Confirm the PunchOut protocol, cart return and document route for this buyer before planning the connection.</p></div>
    <div class="feature-grid">{review.map(([title, description], index) => <article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></article>)}</div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec" id="proof"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Validation</span><h2>Test a real buyer configuration end to end.</h2><p class="lead">Use the buyer’s test environment to check catalog launch, buyer-specific products, cart return into the requisition, approval, approved PO receipt, Shopify order creation and invoice handling. Confirm invoice delivery separately from PunchOut Central’s invoice tracking.</p></div>
    <div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/procurement-systems/"><span>Buyer systems</span><h3>Compatibility overview</h3><p>See how buyer-specific requirements are assessed.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/shopify/"><span>Supplier side</span><h3>Shopify catalog</h3><p>See the current supplier storefront connection.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/how-it-works/"><span>Process</span><h3>Order journey</h3><p>Follow approval, PO, order and invoice.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a></div>
    <p><small>Buyer-side references: <a href="https://www.ivalua.com/press-releases/ivalua-announces-general-availability-of-platform-release-160/">Ivalua’s PunchOut catalog announcement</a> and <a href="https://www.ivalua.com/solutions/process/procure-to-pay/eprocurement-software/">eProcurement overview</a>.</small></p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec soft" id="faq"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">FAQ</span><h2>Ivalua questions</h2></div><div class="faq reveal">
    <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Is every Ivalua buyer using the same PunchOut protocol?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>No universal protocol is assumed here. Confirm this buyer’s cXML or OCI requirements and test them before launch.</p></div></div>
    <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Can the supplier keep Shopify?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>Yes. Shopify or Shopify Plus remains the supplier-hosted catalog; Ivalua is the buyer procurement environment.</p></div></div>
    <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>When is the Shopify order created?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>Only after PunchOut Central receives the approved purchase order, not when the cart returns to the requisition.</p></div></div>
  </div></div></section>
  <section class="page-cta"><div class="wrap reveal"><span class="ey">Confirm an Ivalua setup</span><h2>Bring the buyer’s PunchOut specification.</h2><p class="lead">We can review the catalog, protocol, PO and invoicing requirements against your Shopify store.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Book a demo &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="/integrations/cxml/">Explore cXML</a></div></div></section>
</main>
